Runs on the pinned JDK (reference/JDK_VERSION: OpenJDK 1.8.0_504, the system
/usr/bin/java). The jar is used only as an acceptance check for the new PlantUML
output: `java -jar reference/plantuml.jar -checkonly <file>` must exit 0 for
every non-empty .puml snapshot (empty snapshots belong to crashing fixtures and
are skipped; jar exit codes: 0 ok, 200 parse/render error).

No PlantUML rendering is byte-compared; the jar only proves the generated
files parse. Displayed-text decisions were made visually against the jar's own
PNG renders (§3.11 deviations, also logged in Appendix B at W13):
  1. " is escaped as &#34;, not ~" — the jar rejects ~" inside a quoted
     participant string; &#34; parses in every context (title, participant,
     message, note) and renders as a literal " there. (&quot; parses but
     renders literally, so it is not usable.)
  2. An empty participant label is declared as bare `participant pN` —
     the jar rejects `participant "" as pN`.
